Fundamentals of Vedic Astrology

THE EYE OF THE VEDAS
Jyotishyam = the eye of the Vedas
Most important of the six Vedangas
Gives vision into past, present, and future

THE TRINITY OF KARMA
Sanchita   = accumulated past seeds (storehouse)
Prarabdha  = portion allotted for this birth (fate now)
Aagami     = new actions that plant future seeds

Quote: "Budhee Karmanusaarinee"
The direction of the mind follows one's fate.
Thoughts and decisions ride karmic momentum.

THE COSMIC CLOCK
12 Rasis (signs)
27 Nakshatras (stars), each split into 4 padas
= 108 units that lock the Navamsa chart

9 GRAHAS (planets / variables)
Sun      = soul / father / vitality
Moon     = mind / mother / emotions
Mercury  = intellect / speech / commerce
Venus    = desire / comfort / relationships
Mars     = energy / courage / conflict
Jupiter  = wisdom / guru / expansion
Saturn   = time / restriction / duty
Rahu     = obsession / amplification / foreign
Ketu     = detachment / moksha / past-life residue

12 BHAVAS (houses)
1st  = self / body
7th  = other / partnership
9th  = dharma / fortune
10th = karma / career
(remaining houses follow the same wheel)

MEDICAL ASTROLOGY (RASI-BODY MAP)
Aries     = head
Cancer    = heart / chest
Scorpio   = sex organs
Pisces    = feet

PLANETARY KARAKATWAS (signifiers)
Sun     = father / soul
Moon    = mother / mind
Jupiter = guru / wisdom

PLANET TYPES
Natural Benefics
Jupiter, Venus, Waxing Moon, Mercury
Effect: growth, peace, prosperity

Natural Malefics
Mars, Saturn, Rahu, Ketu, Sun
Effect: aggression, delay, harsh results

"Terrorist" planets (when isolated in a house)
Sun, Saturn, Rahu
They can block or "terrorize" that house's results

FATE VS FREEWILL
Analogy of the cow and rope
Fate   = the rope tied to a staff (birth boundaries)
Freewill = how far the cow walks and which grass it eats
inside that fixed circle

REMEDIES
Nivaarya (amenable karma)
Can be softened by prayer, mantra, gemstones
Turns a fracture into a scratch

Anivarya (fixed karma)
Must be endured
Cannot be cancelled, only understood and lived through

CORE VARIABLES TO READ A CHART
Lagna (ascendant) + Moon sign
Planetary dignity (own / exaltation / debilitation)
House lord placement
Aspects and conjunctions
Dasha periods (timing)
Nakshatra pada (fine-grain destiny unit)
